@host = http://localhost:5000

### The public key, and whether there is one at all. The key is created at startup,
### so this answers both questions: 404 means the active Provider has none yet.
### Paste it into jwt.io next to a token, and watch the kid change when signing
### moves to the YubiHSM.
GET {{host}}/.well-known/jwks.json

### Registration and sign-in are passkey ceremonies: they need an authenticator and
### a secure origin, so they cannot be driven from here. Use the Workshop Frontend.
### These two show the shape only -- the ceremony steps in between are the browser's.
###
###   POST /api/auth/registration-challenge  {username, fullName, role}
###   POST /api/auth/registration            {username, fullName, role, credential}
###   POST /api/auth/sign-in-challenge       {username}
###   POST /api/auth/sign-in                 {username, assertion}

### What a challenge looks like. Safe to call: it creates nothing.
POST {{host}}/api/auth/registration-challenge
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "username": "ada@clinic.example",
  "fullName": "Ada Lovelace",
  "role": "doctor"
}
